findings.comment:
750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) (R) popcorn cart (food debris/dust under popper);
B) (R) sprayer at dish area (buildup in crevice around sprayer surface & general buildup on outer surfaces);
C) (R) walkin cooler shelves (splash/mold);
D) dish machine - general surfaces (edges and doors with lime/buildup);
E) toasters - general surfaces (crumb buildup); 
F) hotbox holding toasters (crumbs on lower ledge); 
G) underside of ice machine - hole where condensate is dripping (mold around opening);   and
H) dish room - underneath clean dish counter (dust buildup - leg bracket, electrical shut off, etc.)

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

findings.citation_text:
750.1220 - A) Floors were soiled in the following areas:
1. (R) under ice machine - puddling water around floor drain where condensate was dripping (some mold growth present around drain and in lid used as small catch basin);
2. (R) walkin cooler - along walls/in corners (food/general debris);
3. (R) corner at steam table and single basin prep sink (food/splash/general debris along the walls/in corner and along baseboard);
4. Floor in dish area (buildup of calcification under machine, around floor drains, and under booster heater).

B) Floor drains and recessed screens in dish room were soiled with buildup of mold/debris.

Clean floors and drains daily/as needed, and maintain them clean.

findings.comment:
750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) inside ice machine - upper ledge behind lid hinge (dust buildup);
B) inside microwave (dried food splash);
C) bottom inside toasters (crumbs);  and
D) inside dish machine (lime and general buildup).

Clean and sanitize food contact surfaces between uses/as needed to prevent cross contamination and eliminate buildup of debris.

750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) oven - general surfaces of doors and around door seals (splash/buildup);
B) plumbing beneath 3 part sink (dust/buildup);
C) popcorn cart (food debris/dust under popper);
D) sprayer in dish area (mold buildup in crevice around sprayer surface);
E) under microwave (food debris/dust);
F) walkin cooler shelves (splash/mold); 
G) drip tubs beneath milk storage in walkin cooler (buildup);
H) hood baffles (general buildup);   and
I) bakers rack in dry storage (dust).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

findings.citation_text:
750.1220 - Floors were soiled in the following areas:
A) under ice machine - puddling water around the floor drain where condensate was dripping (some mold growth present as well);
B) along the walls/in the corner at the steam table and prep sink (food/debris);
C) along the wall in the dish area (food debris and dead ants observed beneath tray return window);
D) behind freezers (debris);   and
E) along walls in walkin cooler (debris).

Clean floors under equipment and along the walls/in corners daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.
Also, clean floor drains as needed. Debris in drains and other areas can serve as a food source for pests.
